	file.0000000000000001.title: "Base Modpack"
	quest.023D641574648661.quest_subtitle: "+0%"
	quest.025414C211C97F7D.quest_desc: [
		"GalleyMaxHealth = 70.0"
		"GalleyMaxSpeed = 40.0"
		"GalleyMaxReverseSpeed = 0.3"
		"GalleyMaxRotationSpeed = 5.0"
		"GalleyAcceleration = 0.015"
		"GalleyRotationAcceleration = 1.0"
		"GalleyContainerSize = 36"
		"GalleyBiome = \"WARM\""
	]
	quest.05E18E634A59D75F.quest_desc: ["■ Most animals only provide resources once a high level of familiarity has been reached."]
	quest.05F608DFB902545F.quest_desc: [
		"■ Unlike vanilla Minecraft, torches in TFC are not permanent: they gradually burn out over time (typically within in-game days) and stop emitting light. They can also be affected by environmental conditions such as rain or snow, which may extinguish them faster."
		""
		"■ Burnt-out torches can be re-lit instead of replaced, and players can also reuse materials (sticks and fire sources) to craft new torches efficiently. Torches are primarily intended as a temporary lighting solution for caves, bases, and early infrastructure before more stable light sources become available."
	]
	quest.075B6A75E9D371B6.quest_desc: [
		"■ Small Ships mod adds a variety of buildable ships for traveling across oceans, rivers, and lakes. Don’t forget to pick up a map so you can create teleportation points. The oceans can be too vast for a regular boat. Transport resources and animals back to your base once you’ve finished your journey. Use a lead to move animals."
		""
		"CogMaxHealth = 20.0"
		"CogMaxSpeed = 35.0"
		"CogMaxReverseSpeed = 0.1"
		"CogMaxRotationSpeed = 5.0"
		"CogAcceleration = 0.005"
		"CogRotationAcceleration = 0.7"
		"CogContainerSize = 9"
		"CogBiome = \"NEUTRAL\""
	]
	quest.09A84C873373D431.quest_desc: ["■ Domesticated wool-bearing animals can be used to produce material for weaving."]
	quest.0D09F25554851376.quest_subtitle: "Moistens the soil layer above it"
	quest.10C72896AD0E9B2D.quest_desc: ["■ Kaolin clay can only be found in very hot, humid biomes or in very small quantities near structures. Ordinary clay, on the other hand, is found everywhere and is marked by specific plants."]
	quest.1491B36E817E69F8.quest_desc: ["■ Use this as a small backpack for carrying items. You should also put small pieces of ore in here and place them back in the smelter/pit to make basic alloys. But don’t carry more than 5 pots of items, or you’ll be overweight."]
	quest.14938880540EFE0F.quest_desc: ["■ Can’t find a specific gem or ore after playing for a while? Trade your food for the minerals and ores you need with the goblin merchant, who appears below depth level 60."]
	quest.17726FD9F6903311.quest_desc: [
		"■ Storing food in a large, sealed vessel extends its shelf life."
		""
		"■ If there are spoiled foods in there, they will attract pests, which will cause other foods to spoil more quickly."
	]
	quest.17E291702488A8F3.quest_subtitle: "+10%"
	quest.1AF848C18BC07BB6.quest_desc: ["■ Near underground magma at the deepest levels, you can encounter vicious blaze-dragons that drop Dragon’s Breath and Blaze Rods."]
	quest.1C2D881C6C5EA79E.quest_desc: ["■ Attach the head to the stick, and you’ll have your first primitive tool."]
	quest.23DDE3EFBDCF1237.quest_desc: ["■ The most efficient and fastest, but also the most resource-intensive, way to travel is via Waystone."]
	quest.249CA81A1AEC6E53.quest_desc: [
		"■ Positive qualities of a good base location:"
		""
		"- Source of gray clay for pottery.                    "
		"- Source of pink clay for blacksmithing."
		""
		"- A source of fresh water, preferably a river for powering waterwheels."
		""
		"- Forest for logging."
		""
		"- Mollisol soil for the most efficient farming."
		"{image:tfc:block/crop/green_bean_2_stick width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		""
		"- Ocean nearby for fast travel by ship."
		""
		"- Hot spring to supply therapeutic baths via aqueducts."
		""
		""
		"- Warm, humid mountainous biome, allowing crops to be grown at different elevations with varying temperatures and humidity."
		""
		"- White chalk mountains with graphite deposits in caves for blacksmithing."
		""
		"- Ore veins"
		"{image:tfc:item/metal/horse_armor/wrought_iron width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.264C20959AD73B3B.quest_desc: [
		"■ The TerraFirmaCraft mod has been around for 13 years and has acquired a huge amount of polished content during that time. Many Dragon Survival fans have always wanted to combine these two mods, but it required a lot of effort and for a long time they were not compatible. Now, thanks to this modpack, you can enjoy both mods together!"
		""
		"■ Try your hand at primitive survival with Terrafirmacraft and playable dragons from Dragon Survival in 1.21.1! If you've never tried either mod before, you shouldn't have much trouble getting started here. I've tried to put as many hints as possible everywhere, and TFC's built-in wiki will be your guide to this brave new world. Welcome to Terra Draconis!"
		""
		"■ Link to modpack (1378576): https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/modpacks/tfc-terra-draconis-primitive-dragon-survival"
		"{@pagebreak}"
	]
	quest.264C20959AD73B3B.title: "Play As Dragon"
	quest.26C41CA49E46BFDC.quest_desc: ["■ Cut the berry bushes with a knife to harvest the cuttings. The larger bushes are very prickly, so be careful."]
	quest.2C7F4B37FA136930.quest_subtitle: "+20%"
	quest.2CEE9EAA0B79F5C6.quest_desc: [
		"■ To obtain dragon wings and the ability to fly, you must complete the Ocean Dragon quest chain. It is NPC what will ask you for various materials, and at the end of the 10th quest, he will give you a special item that allows you to craft wings."
		""
		"■ Even if you can’t find the structures, there will always be a way to reach them! For example, the underground goblin sells maps for the quest dragon and various dungeons. And if that doesn’t work out, you can craft a quest dragon spawn egg yourself. The same goes for the keys to Dragon Survival structures."
	]
	quest.2CEE9EAA0B79F5C6.title: "Wings"
	quest.2D07C172C503D1BF.quest_desc: [
		"■ Place it in a wet biome to get as much compost as possible."
		""
		"■ In addition to compost, there are many other types of fertilizer."
	]
	quest.2FE03BAD90DE50E9.quest_desc: ["■ Unfired pots are useless until you fire them."]
	quest.31709EBCCFF3D23C.quest_desc: ["■ You can put a chest or a barrel on a mule or a donkey."]
	quest.31FBAC8FC214EDA7.quest_desc: [
		"■ Temperature is the main mechanic of Cold Sweat. Like hunger and health, it must be monitored and properly managed. When the player's core temperature reaches a critical point, either too low or too high, the player will begin to take damage and eventually die."
		""
		"■ The player's body temperature ranges from between -150 and 150. Note that this range is arbitrary, and doesn't correspond to any real-life temperature unit. 0 is neutral, and anything more than 100 or less than -100 is deadly. This is represented by an icon in the middle of the player's hotbar."
		"{image:cold_sweat:textures/mob_effect/grace.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		"■  It is affected by:"
		"- The temperature of biomes bear the player"
		"- Nearby blocks, such as lava or ice"
		"- The time of day"
		"- The current season "
		"- The player's depth underground"
		"- Wetness, caused by water or rain"
		"- Hot items in hand"
		""
		"{image:cold_sweat:item/thermometer/thermometer width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		"■ If a thermometer is equipped in the player's hotbar, or as a curio, a more advanced temperature readout will be displayed."
		""
	]
	quest.39FF6BD4F4327663.quest_desc: [
		"■ If you've ever wanted races on your server with friends to be more than just conditional or implemented on command blocks, Dragon Rings mod is for you! You can use multiple rings to create routes, make locked rooms with redstone, calculate the exact time it takes to complete the track, reward winners, and much more."
		""
		"■ Use guidebook in English, Chinese, Polish and Russian that provides detailed information on all the intricacies of building your dream track."
	]
	quest.39FF6BD4F4327663.title: "Dragon Rings"
	quest.3AE96378EA10298A.quest_desc: ["■ Craft the Witherkiller sword to collect Wither Skeleton skulls with a 100% drop chance. These black skeletons spawn deep within the caves."]
	quest.3BCD0AA825E13F2D.quest_desc: [
		"DrakkarMaxHealth = 70.0"
		"DrakkarMaxSpeed = 50.0"
		"DrakkarMaxReverseSpeed = 0.3"
		"DrakkarMaxRotationSpeed = 5.0"
		"DrakkarAcceleration = 0.015"
		"DrakkarRotationAcceleration = 1.0"
		"DrakkarContainerSize = 18"
		"DrakkarBiome = \"COLD\""
	]
	quest.3BD0767C0E9B1FE1.quest_desc: ["■ A balanced backpack from the Sophisticated mod has been tuned for progression - you’ll be able to craft it once you learn leatherworking!"]
	quest.40208F3039C413A0.quest_desc: [
		"■ Charcoal (TerraFirmaCraft) is produced using a charcoal pit: wood logs are stacked in a sealed structure, covered with blocks, and ignited. After a full burn cycle without exposure to air, the logs convert into charcoal."
		""
		"■ Common mistakes:"
		""
		"- Leaving gaps in the pit cover, which causes the fire to fail or burn normally instead of producing charcoal."
		""
		"- Opening the pit too early, interrupting the conversion process."
		""
		"- Use of loose or flaming blocks for covering. The ground could collapse and destroy some of the coal."
	]
	quest.412E6BDF497DECA5.quest_subtitle: "Dries out the soil layer above it"
	quest.41C113F56B942DE5.quest_desc: [
		"■ River: sugar - clay ball"
		""
		"■ Farmer: sylvite - saltpeter - rotten compost - guano - kelp shearer"
		""
		"■ Hunter: turtle - rotten flesh - bone - turtle scute"
		""
		"■ Icy: snowball - ice - frost relic"
		""
		"■ Wild: sand - mortar"
		""
		"■ Architect: flint - glue - nautilus shell - swim bladder"
		""
		"■ Blacksmith: sea urchin - mollusk - clam - mussel - bituminous coal - depth nugget"
		""
		"■ Cavern: glow ink sac - gunpowder - nautilus shell "
		""
		"■ Collector: ink sac - goat horn - native gold - native copper - native silver - name tag - recovery compass - snatcherfish"
		""
		"■ Coral: live corals"
	]
	quest.42430371C7B0FBE2.quest_desc: [
		"■ With at least 2 stones in hand, right click to make stone tools. You can find the correct form in the book or on JEI."
		""
		"■ There are all kinds of rocks just lying around at your feet."
	]
	quest.425977833402985C.quest_desc: ["■ Birds lay eggs in their nests. If there are males in the pen, they will fertilize the females, and the new eggs will be fertilized."]
	quest.4806CC7B66EA1751.quest_desc: ["■ Floating balloons have been added high in the sky to give you something. You can try shooting them down with a spear or arrows!"]
	quest.481D8683937CDE6B.quest_subtitle: "+10%"
	quest.490A458178A80D92.quest_desc: ["■ You can summon and defeat the Wither Boss. Soul Sand can be found in one of the structures or crafted."]
	quest.4B1CA30A7538097B.quest_subtitle: "+10%"
	quest.4C877C6B418661B3.quest_desc: [
		"■ Absolutely all standard dragons and creatures from the modpack have been completely revamped. Most of them have new abilities and debuffs. Read the ability descriptions and tooltips for more information."
		""
		"■ To change your dragon and appearance, use the altar."
	]
	quest.4C877C6B418661B3.title: "Dragons!"
	quest.4D08CFD2157C8D20.quest_desc: ["■ You can use these stones to make decorations and bricks"]
	quest.4E5CB99C69A5B558.quest_subtitle: "-20%"
	quest.4FB909F85F5CC694.quest_desc: ["The best way to use milk is to turn it into cheese."]
	quest.51D1CA5AA22874CA.quest_desc: [
		"■ A stone pickaxe isn't suitable for mining ore and stone. You'll need to create an alloy and pour it into a mold. "
		""
		"■ Hurry up and pour the molten metal into the mold! Otherwise, it will solidify and you'll have to reheat the whole thing."
	]
	quest.51F5C7CF937410B6.quest_desc: [
		"■ Armor can be insulated to reduce the effects of extreme temperatures on the player. There is a variety of insulation items that can be mixed to provide optimal protection against the player's environment. Insulation items are applied at the sewing table. If the player wishes to remove insulation, shears can be placed in the insulation slot, removing one insulation item at a time starting from the most recently added item and working backwards."
		""
		"- Cold ( Blue ) - Slows the rate at which the player freezes in the cold."
		""
		"- Hot ( Orange ) - Slows the rate at which the player overheats in the heat. "
		""
		"- Neutral ( Purple ) - Provides an equal, but less powerful, amount of both hot and cold insulation."
		""
		"■ There is one more special kind of adaptive ( Green ) insulation, which slowly changes its properties to become either hot or cold depending on the player's environment. Adaptive insulation is slightly less effective than normal hot/cold insulation."
	]
	quest.547A6B4B511C6B0B.quest_desc: ["■ Hold down CTRL on any item in TFC to learn how to use or craft it. "]
	quest.556196E03E50666D.quest_desc: ["■ Ingenious thinking makes it possible to create unique chests that take up little space and offer additional features. It will take some effort to build them."]
	quest.56A3A6FA1CC0DB81.quest_desc: ["■ To get the most out of your garden beds, it’s best to plant new crop groups every year. Just like in real life. This is called “crop rotation.”"]
	quest.571EC755BF5C215C.quest_desc: ["■ These sticks ignite slowly and only with a small chance of success, but they are very cheap."]
	quest.584A6D43433E2A8C.quest_desc: [
		"■ As a dragon ages, a new problem may arise in addition to having a large health pool. Being huge is a source of pride, but it also makes it difficult to fit into small spaces."
		""
		"■ If you’re tired of crouching down and trying to squeeze through doorways, craft Star Bones to rejuvenate yourself. To stop growing, use Star Hearts."
	]
	quest.5B24EF91010E0CB6.quest_desc: [
		"BriggMaxHealth = 450.0"
		"BriggMaxSpeed = 45.0"
		"BriggMaxReverseSpeed = 0.1"
		"BriggMaxRotationSpeed = 4.0"
		"BriggAcceleration = 0.015"
		"BriggRotationAcceleration = 0.55"
		"BriggContainerSize = 54"
		"BriggBiome = \"NEUTRAL\""
	]
	quest.5BA7CF3EC0E6F73E.quest_desc: [
		"■ In TerraFirmaCraft, a firepit is not crafted but created through the interaction of in-game items."
		""
		"- Drop (Q) 3 sticks and 1 log on a single block;"
		""
		"- Add up to 5 units of kindling (straw, paper, etc.) to increase the chance of ignition;"
		""
		"- Then use a firestarter on that spot until it successfully ignites."
		""
		"■ Once lit, a firepit appears, which serves as a heat source and is used for basic recipes (such as torches and cooking food)."
		""
		"■ If the items are not placed on a single block or if there is no log, the firepit will not be created."
	]
	quest.5BD9A6A377ECC376.quest_desc: [
		"■ Via Romana mod adds a transportation network inspired by ancient Roman infrastructure."
		""
		"■ The mod also allows the construction of water routes, extending transportation across rivers, lakes, and seas. By combining land roads and water connections, players can establish efficient trade and travel networks across large distances."
		""
		"■ Right-click with the Charting Map to learn more."
		""
		"■ Open a standard map - M button."
	]
	quest.5C826F44ADD54DB8.quest_desc: [
		"■ To obtain an anvil stone, you need to find a suitable solid rock and remove all the blocks surrounding the target stone. It will then collapse on its own, giving you the raw version."
		""
		"■ Place the stone in the correct spot and tap the top edge with a hammer."
	]
	quest.608054EC75925A9F.quest_desc: ["■ You can make a stone anvil out of these stones"]
	quest.6175B1AD78636D75.quest_desc: [
		"■ The Configurable KeepInventory mod keeps your hotbar when you die."
		""
		"■ Inventory Profiles Next is a powerful inventory management mod that lets you sort items, move matching items, dump all items into a chest with a single click, and lock slots to protect specific gear. It also features Profiles, allowing you to save and instantly swap full gear sets (equipment and hotbar) using custom hotkeys"
	]
	quest.669800F30AE47B55.quest_desc: ["■ Track Rings"]
	quest.66B98612EBA51F61.quest_desc: ["■ For creating track"]
	quest.66E9BB5606F0E15B.quest_desc: ["■ Different types of soil provide different bonuses for growing plants. The best one is mollisol."]
	quest.678A069F7F58936C.quest_desc: [
		"{image:extremesoundmuffler:textures/gui/sm_gui_dark.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		"In a human player's inventory, you can turn off repetitive, annoying sounds. For example, you can turn off the mooing of cows or the bleating of sheep."
	]
	quest.6D96546FF7ECC2AB.quest_desc: ["■ Unfired pots are useless until you fire them."]
	quest.6E2314DA9B351046.quest_desc: [
		"■ All dragons have the same diet to maintain TerraFirmaCraft's complex system of nutrients and thirst."
		""
		"■ The more varied your diet is, the healthier you’ll be. Check the nutritional information on all your food and try to eat only fresh items to avoid food poisoning."
	]
	quest.6E2314DA9B351046.title: "Food"
	quest.6EFDC79D53FCCCA0.quest_desc: ["■ With at least 5 clays in hand, right click to knap clay. Check the recipes in JEI by pressing R and U on an item."]
	quest.7060D92564116550.quest_desc: [
		"■ To place items on the ground, press the V key. This acts as a storage area where items won’t disappear. "
		""
		"■ Also, if you place unfired clay items in a 1x1 dirt hole, you can surround them with 8 straws and 8 logs to fire them."
	]
	quest.726306413DD75965.quest_desc: ["■ To propagate fruit trees, you need to cut off their branches with axe. Don’t cut these trees down to the ground, or you won’t get anything."]
	quest.73D27F9E1669552E.quest_desc: ["■ Many animals may want to kill you in these harsh environments.  It's best not to let them get too close to you."]
	quest.7820453FFBA954B5.quest_desc: ["■ Rabbits and pigs can eat expired food"]
	quest.786E22700E0717ED.quest_desc: [
		"■ Negative qualities of the area:"
		""
		"- A hot or cold climate will make farming more difficult and require specialized clothing."
		""
		"- Only salt water is available."
		""
		"- Volcanoes may erupt, so it is best to avoid them."
		""
		"- A small island."
	]
	quest.796E48CED5B9FFFE.quest_subtitle: "-10%"
	quest.79F1F968521D5F12.quest_subtitle: "-10%"
	quest.7DAEEAD15C53752A.quest_desc: [
		"■ For more information on progression in the mod, check the TFC guidebook in your inventory (book button) or use the item book."
		""
		"■ For Servers: In server.properties, You need to change the level-type to enable TFC world generation: tfc\\:overworld"
	]
	quest.7FA497B541119918.quest_desc: [
		"■ TerraFirmaCraft (TFC) is a total conversion mod that overhauls and reinvents survival mode. The goal of the mod is to create a believable, challenging survival experience, in a brand new immersive setting. It completely overhauls Minecraft world generation - from adding continents, to flowing rivers, to mountain ranges, to varied and diverse forests, flora, and fauna. Below is a list of some of the features of this mod:"
		""
		"- The underground has been completely reimagined, with layers of different types of rock, and massive sparse ore deposits of several different types."
		""
		"- A fully fledged technology tree, from pottery and pit kilns, to charcoal production, producing iron with a bloomery, steel making and more."
		""
		"- Seasons, weather, and a realistic climate and calendar model cause the player to need to stockpile food for winter to survive."
		""
		"- The world is alive, with many different plants, wild crops, wild fruits, animals - both passive and predators - to find."
		""
		"- The player must manage their food's expiration, nutrition, and thirst using our detailed food and cooking mechanics."
		""
		"■  In order to understand all of these new features, TerraFirmaCraft comes with a detailed in-game Field Guide, which is available from the moment you spawn in, and will guide you through the art of surviving in this brand-new world."
		"{image:dragonsurvival:textures/ability_effect/fire_immunity.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7FA497B541119918.title: "Terra Draconis"
